  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The outcomes in the problem are 6000, 0 (from Lottery A) and 3000, 0 (from Lottery B). Ignoring probabilities, the set of all outcomes is {6000, 0, 3000, 0}. The mean of these outcomes—the aspiration level—is (6000 + 0 + 3000 + 0) / 4 = 2250 Euros. Next, for each lottery, we evaluate the probability that its outcomes exceed this aspiration level (i.e., positive differences from 2250). For Lottery A: 6000 > 2250 (positive difference), occurring with 45%; 0 < 2250 (negative), with 55%. So, the probability of a positive difference is 45%. For Lottery B: 3000 > 2250 (positive), with 90%; 0 < 2250 (negative), with 10%. So, the probability of a positive difference is 90%. Since the reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences, it would prefer Lottery B (90% > 45%).",
